{
  "work_package_id": "WP-003",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-004.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-001"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "`name-mapping.json` includes `model`, `model_slug`, `cc_model`, and `suite` fields in each entry after a build",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`name-mapping.json` covers all three persona suites — not just ledger",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Standalone and ledger-support entries have `number: null` and `suite` set to `\"standalone\"` or `\"ledger-support\"` respectively",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`role` for non-ledger personas is derived by stripping the suite suffix from the persona `name` field (e.g., `\"Developer (Standalone)\"` → `\"Developer\"`)",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "For standalone and ledger-support suites, when no model override exists, the entry resolves to `model: \"Inherit / Auto\"`, `model_slug: \"inherit\"`, `cc_model: \"inherit\"`",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The `AGENT_NAMES` constant in `constants.ts` only includes ledger entries — standalone entries with colliding role names (e.g., `\"Developer\"`) do not overwrite ledger entries",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The model resolution in `build-personas.js` follows the same priority chain as the build plugin: `assignments.json` > per-persona YAML > `_shared.yaml` default",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The `NameMappingEntry` interface accommodates the new fields and widened types without breaking existing consumers",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Model resolution tests pass",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T13:49:55Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T13:58:17Z",
      "duration_ms": 502000,
      "summary": [
        "Implemented multi-suite name-mapping generation and model resolution in build-personas.js, updated NameMappingEntry interface in constants.ts, and created comprehensive model resolution tests. Key changes: (1) Extracted model resolution logic into scripts/lib/persona-model-resolution.js as a standalone importable module with loadModelRegistry() and resolveModel(); (2) Extended build-personas.js name-mapping pass to cover all three suites (ledger, standalone, ledger-support) with model/model_slug/cc_model/suite fields; (3) Added deriveRole() to strip suite suffixes from persona names; (4) Updated NameMappingEntry interface with widened number/role types and new optional fields; (5) Added .filter(e => !e.suite || e.suite === 'ledger') to AGENT_NAMES construction; (6) Fixed a pre-existing parseYamlScalars bug where quoted values followed by inline comments were not properly unquoted; (7) Wrote 17 passing unit tests covering all priority chain cases, inherit skip behavior, partial assignments, and loadModelRegistry file-loading scenarios."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "scripts/build-personas.js",
          "mcp-server/src/utils/constants.ts",
          "scripts/lib/persona-model-resolution.js",
          "scripts/tests/build-personas-model-resolution.test.js",
          "personas/name-mapping.json"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:50:00Z",
          "note": "parseYamlScalars() in build-personas.js had a pre-existing bug: quoted scalar values followed by an inline YAML comment (e.g., `key: \"value\"  # comment`) were not correctly unquoted because the endsWith('\"') check failed when the trailing comment followed the closing quote. The fix changes the strategy to detect the opening quote first, find the matching closing quote, and extract the content — rather than relying on startsWith/endsWith symmetry. This was latent for the original 7 scalar fields but surfaced immediately with default_model and default_model_slug from _shared.yaml."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:50:00Z",
          "note": "The model resolution helper (scripts/lib/persona-model-resolution.js) is now a standalone ESM module importable by both build-personas.js and tests. The same resolution logic was previously duplicated inline inside the if (!CHECK) block — extracting it to a module improves testability and eliminates the duplication."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:50:00Z",
          "note": "The non-ledger entries in name-mapping.json are sorted alphabetically by suite then role. This ensures stable diff output across builds, but the ledger entries sort by number (as before). A future reader of the file will notice mixed sort strategies — a comment in build-personas.js documents this intent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T13:58:47Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T14:02:53Z",
      "duration_ms": 246000,
      "summary": [
        "All 9 acceptance criteria verified. Build compiles cleanly (tsc --noEmit PASS). All 107 tests pass including the 17 model resolution unit tests. name-mapping.json contains 40 entries: 9 ledger + 10 ledger-support + 21 standalone. Every entry carries model, model_slug, cc_model, suite fields (AC-1). All three suites present (AC-2). Non-ledger entries have number: null (AC-3). Role derivation strips suffixes correctly — no '(Standalone)' or '(Ledger Support)' in any role field (AC-4). All non-ledger entries resolve to Inherit / Auto sentinel (AC-5, expected since no assignments.json or per-YAML model in dev environment). AGENT_NAMES filter correctly excludes the 'Developer (Standalone)' entry and 30 other non-ledger entries — AGENT_NAMES contains exactly 9 ledger entries (AC-6). Priority chain integration tested with a live assignments.json: per-persona assignment wins, inherit skip falls through to YAML, default_model_uuid applies to unspecified personas (AC-7). NameMappingEntry widened types compile without errors and downstream consumers (workflow-handoff.ts) only access target sub-fields unaffected by the type widening (AC-8). parseYamlScalars bug fix for quoted+commented YAML scalars verified correct — Claude Sonnet 4.6 correctly parsed from _shared.yaml."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "17 model resolution unit tests + 90 regression tests",
        "tests_passed": 107,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:02:53Z",
          "note": "scripts/lib/persona-model-resolution.js loadModelRegistry(): when local.json (or default.json) parses successfully but contains a non-array JSON value (e.g., {}), the code silently skips it without emitting a warning. The try/catch only catches parse errors. A warn() call when !Array.isArray(parsed) would improve diagnosability for misconfigured registry files. This is low risk since the graceful degradation is correct — no crash, no bad data."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:02:53Z",
          "note": "No coverage gap for the case where a persona's YAML model_slug is a valid slug but has no entry in the registry (slugToEntry miss). The resolveModel() code falls back to using the slug itself as the model name and 'inherit' as cc_model — correct behavior, verified via Edge Case in this QA pass. A test for this path would improve completeness."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-07-21T13:49:55Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-21T14:02:53Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:58:17Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 9 acceptance criteria met. Key test surface: scripts/tests/build-personas-model-resolution.test.js covers all 5 priority chain levels, inherit-skip behavior at levels 1 and 3, partial assignments, and loadModelRegistry file loading/graceful degradation (17 tests). The build emits 40 entries (9 ledger + 31 non-ledger). TypeScript compiles cleanly (tsc --noEmit). A pre-existing parseYamlScalars bug was fixed as part of this implementation (quoted+commented YAML scalars weren't unquoted correctly). QA should verify: (1) that the AGENT_NAMES filter correctly excludes non-ledger entries from the constants map, (2) that a build with a present assignments.json correctly overrides model fields in the generated name-mapping.json, and (3) that the TypeScript widened types (number | null, string for role) do not create type errors in downstream consumers of NameMappingEntry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:02:53Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 9 ACs met and verified through code review, runtime execution, integration tests, and edge-case analysis. 107/107 tests pass with zero regressions. Key verified behaviors: (1) AGENT_NAMES filter is .filter(e => !e.suite || e.suite === 'ledger') — correctly excludes 31 non-ledger entries including the 'Developer (Standalone)' collision; (2) priority chain integration-tested with a live assignments.json against the real model-registry/default.json; (3) parseYamlScalars quoted+comment fix confirmed working for both default_model and default_model_slug from _shared.yaml. Two low-priority observations recorded as comments — neither is a blocker."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

